    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> be the origin and the position vector of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></math>. If the position vectors of the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, then the projection of the vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> on a vector perpendicular to the vectors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is",
